title: Role::HTTP should point at API::Docker's TIMEOUTS section
updated: 2026-08-28T00:26:18Z
---

karr #72 added a =head1 TIMEOUTS to lib/API/Docker.pm saying once what a bound
covers and what it does not -- idle time on reads, connecting, neither on
writing, and SO_RCVTIMEO measuring the underlying receives under TLS rather
than plaintext arrival -- plus where a bound applies, including the pre-flight
requests and version negotiation.

It went into API::Docker rather than into Role::HTTP next to the read_timeout
attribute, only because Role::HTTP was locked for karr #64 at the time.

Role::HTTP is where a reader of read_timeout/connect_timeout lands. Two lines
would close the loop, one under each attribute:

  See L<API::Docker/"What a timeout covers"> for what the bound covers, and
  L<API::Docker/"Where a bound applies"> for which calls carry it.

Nothing in the new section duplicates Role::HTTP's own "Bounding a request
that never ends" / "Bounding the connection itself" measurements; it
summarises them and links to them.
